WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.181
FedRAMP stands for the Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program.

2
00:00:04.181 --> 00:00:14.158
It is a United States government program that standardizes security assessment, authorization, and continuous monitoring for cloud services used by federal agencies.

3
00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:16.314
The basic purpose is consistency.

4
00:00:16.314 --> 00:00:24.915
Before FedRAMP, agencies could evaluate cloud services in different ways, which created duplicated work and uneven expectations.

5
00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:31.989
FedRAMP gives agencies, cloud providers, assessors, and stakeholders a shared process and vocabulary.

6
00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:38.614
FedRAMP matters because federal agencies rely on cloud services to support mission and business functions.

7
00:00:38.614 --> 00:00:48.392
Those services may process, store, or transmit government information, so agencies need a structured way to understand and manage cloud security risk.

8
00:00:48.392 --> 00:00:51.765
FedRAMP is not simply a form or a product label.

9
00:00:51.765 --> 00:01:03.468
It combines security controls, documentation, independent assessment, authorization decisions, and ongoing monitoring into a repeatable program for federal cloud risk management.

10
00:01:03.468 --> 00:01:11.640
A cloud service provider may use FedRAMP to demonstrate that its cloud offering has been assessed against common federal security expectations.

11
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.060
Agencies can then use that information as part of their own risk decisions.

12
00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:22.905
The program is built on NIST guidance, especially NIST SP 800-53 security controls.

13
00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:29.191
That connection helps FedRAMP align with broader federal information security and risk management practices.

14
00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:33.342
This course provides an educational overview of FedRAMP concepts.

15
00:01:33.342 --> 00:01:40.356
It should not be used as professional legal, compliance, authorization, assessment, or regulatory direction.

16
00:01:40.356 --> 00:01:44.617
The most useful way to think about FedRAMP is as a shared trust mechanism.

17
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:52.489
It gives cloud providers, federal agencies, and assessors a common way to organize evidence and discuss security posture.
